---
description: Keep branching and sequencing visible; do not bury decisions in combinators or implicit pipelines
alwaysApply: true
---

# Do not hide control flow

A reader must see when a flip is skipped and when an order is submitted. Do not bury those branches in combinators, implicit pipelines, or helpers whose names hide a decision. Wire collaborators at the edge (factory-functions.mdc). Do not invent a pipeline framework to hide a loop.

```typescript
type Grid = { readonly breakPrice: number; readonly flipped: boolean };
type SubmitFlip = (grid: Grid) => void;

// ❌ The skip lives inside when(). Callers cannot see the branch.
function when(predicate: (grid: Grid) => boolean, submit: SubmitFlip): SubmitFlip {
    return function maybeSubmit(grid: Grid): void {
        if (predicate(grid)) {
            submit(grid);
        }
    };
}

// ✅ Sequence and branch are on the page.
function flipIfBroken(grid: Grid, currentPrice: number, submitFlip: SubmitFlip): void {
    if (currentPrice < grid.breakPrice || grid.flipped) {
        return;
    }
    submitFlip(grid);
}
```

Named `if` and early `return` are the feature. `map`/`filter` are fine when they do not hide a domain decision.
